# Canonical identity for the repository owner.
#
# Git records an author name+email verbatim on every commit, so the same
# person appears as several contributors when the local git config changes
# between machines or sessions. These three spellings are one person:
#
#   Michael Song        <red3rdeye@gmail.com>   (328 commits)
#   Michael Warren Song <red3rdeye@gmail.com>   ( 26 commits)
#   CYLIC-AMP           <Red3rdeye@gmail.com>   (  3 commits, capital R)
#
# The capital R in the third makes git treat it as a distinct address.
# This file folds all three into one for git log, git shortlog and
# git blame. It does NOT alter any commit object, and GitHub's web UI
# does not read .mailmap -- it is a local/clone-level normalization only.

Michael Song <red3rdeye@gmail.com> <Red3rdeye@gmail.com>
Michael Song <red3rdeye@gmail.com> Michael Warren Song <red3rdeye@gmail.com>
Michael Song <red3rdeye@gmail.com> CYLIC-AMP <Red3rdeye@gmail.com>
